{
  "strategy": "OPENING/LAND-GRAB (2110): six colonisers in flight, the twin Spore Cloud drives west to germanium-rich Groombridge 34, dry Santa Maria #9 crawls at free warp 2 to Kapteyn's Star, Santa Maria #11 splits its run warp4-then-warp3 to reach Wolf 359 without stranding, and Gliese 1 alternates colonisers with its first real factory batch.",
  "memo": "IRON FIST - MEMO (2110). PHASE: OPENING / LAND-GRAB. WIN = 60 PLANETS; I hold 2, six colonisers are in flight, 12 unowned known, 75 stars unscanned. Exploration and fuel remain the binding constraints.\n\nFUEL LAW (empirical - trust it over intuition): w4 fuel/ly = mass x 0.020. w3 = mass x 0.0067 (one third). w1-2 = FREE. w5 costs as much as w6 = BANNED. ALWAYS compute distance x mass x 0.02 BEFORE issuing a w4 waypoint. NEW TRICK: if the tank cannot cover a full w4 run, SPLIT THE LEG - w4 to an [x,y] point that spends ~90% of the tank, then w3 to the target. Beats a pure w3 run by ~2 years and never strands. Ranges on a full tank: Scout(25) 600 ly at w4; Spore Cloud loaded(42) 178 ly; Spore Cloud x2 loaded(84) 178 ly; Santa Maria loaded(95) 105 ly. SPORE CLOUD IS THE COLONISER - 22 res, 1000 colonists, 70% more reach than the 30-res Santa Maria. Build no more Santa Marias.\n\nSTATE: Gliese 1 (188,192) pop 63,000, 12/63 fact, 10/63 mine, 75 res, STARBASE - the empire's ONLY refuelling point; that is a strategic weakness. Shaula (236,177) pop 19,400, 0/19 fact, 10/19 mine, 19 res, surface germanium 2 kT so factories stall there; mines to cap (19) first, always.\n\nIN FLIGHT: SM#10 lands Rasalhague 95% in 2111. SM#11 split-leg to Wolf 359 93%, lands ~2113. SC#12 -> Betelgeuse ~2113. SC#13 -> Deneb ~2115. SC#14 -> Mimosa ~2116. SC#15 (TWO hulls, one fleet - cannot split) -> Groombridge 34, germanium conc 96, lands ~2117. SM#9 dry, free w2 -> Kapteyn's Star, lands ~2121.\n\nREMAINING TARGETS from Gliese 1: Megrez 156 ly (hab 0%, best left), Zaurak 122, Merak 124, Wolf 1061 161, Kochab 200 (deep in e2 space). Also UNEXPLORED and CLOSE: Sabik 33 ly, Phecda 45, Rana 76, Gliese 1061 - a new Long Range Scout is queued to check Sabik first; a habitable world 33 ly out would be worth more than any -4% rock.\n\nRESEARCH: 30% Propulsion -> Prop 5 (Daddy Long Legs 7, +range empire-wide). Highest leverage unlock in the game for me; every extra ly of coloniser reach is a planet. Then Construction, then Biotech. Weapons only when an e2 warship appears.\n\nQUEUES: Gliese 1 = Spore Cloud x2, Long Range Scout, Armed Probe, Factory x10, Spore Cloud x2, Factory x15. Gliese 1 is only 12/63 factories - that underbuild is now costing ~50 res/yr; fix it. Shaula = Mine x9 (to cap), Factory x10.\n\nSTANDING RULES: 1. w4 when the tank covers it, split-leg when tight, w2 when dry, never w5. 2. Load colonists the same turn the hull is built. 3. Three colonisers in the pipe at all times. 4. Scouts fly w3 unless the tank is over 60%. 5. Take worlds, never glass them; negative hab still counts. 6. Escorts are Armed Probes (26 res), not Destroyers (60). 7. Second starbase at Rasalhague or Betelgeuse the moment either clears 25 res - it doubles effective empire reach.\n\nTHREATS: e2 Armed Probe #1 is sitting IN ORBIT of Shaula (236,177) - Shaula has zero defenses and my armed probe is 8 years out. e2 scouts at (273,166), (285,287), (341,156) are mapping my lanes. e2 holds 2 planets, tech 2, 0 capships. Homeworld bearing NE near (360,76). OPEN: Wormhole Alpha and 1 storm unlocated.",
  "observations": [
    "Fuel burn is far harsher than the original Stars!: a loaded Santa Maria (mass 95) burns roughly 1.9 fuel per light year at warp 4, giving a 200-tank hull only ~105 ly of range. Nearly every colony ship I launch strands short of its target. Either the engine fuel table or the mass-times-distance factor looks miscalibrated.",
    "Warp 5 costs the same fuel per ly as warp 6 in my measurements, so warp 5 is strictly dominated and there is never a reason to use it. Looks like an off-by-one in the fuel-usage table lookup.",
    "A fleet that exhausts its fuel drops to warp 0 and stays there permanently, even though warps 1-2 cost zero fuel. It should coast at the highest free warp instead of stopping dead - as it stands, running dry is effectively ship loss.",
    "Duplicate and endlessly repeating fuel messages: every turn I get both '[Fuel] X has run out of fuel and dropped to warp 0.' and '[Fuel] X has run out of fuel.' for the same ship, and they keep firing year after year for fleets that are stationary with no orders (Stalwart Defender #1 has produced these for 5 consecutive turns).",
    "Newly built ships of the same design auto-merge into a single fleet (Spore Cloud #15 came out as 'Spore Cloudx2') and there is no way to split them, so a colonise order consumes both colony ships on one planet. Two 22-resource hulls buy one planet instead of two.",
    "Every fleet's waypoint list carries a leading pseudo-waypoint 'Space at <current x,y>@w6' that I never issued. It appears to be the current position echoed back at warp 6 and it clutters the order list.",
    "Enemy score reports tech=2 versus my tech=18 after 10 turns from an identical start, while their resources (75) exceed mine (67). The opposing AI appears not to be researching at all, which makes the tech-victory condition trivially uncontested."
  ],
